header>\n    <div class=\"top-strip\">\n      <div><span class=\"accent\">Last chance</span> Get up to <em>40% off</em> a print subscription</div>\n      <div class=\"see-page\">See page 57</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <section class=\"promotions\">\n      <div class=\"promo-cover-wrap\">\n        <figure class=\"cover-one placeholder\" aria-label=\"The New Review sports-film cover\">\n          <div class=\"review\">The Observer<br><strong>the new review</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"cover-figures\">[Montage: sports-film scenes]</div>\n          <div class=\"cover-title\">\n            A LEAGUE OF THEIR OWN\n            <span class=\"cover-subtitle\">GUY LODGE CHOOSES THE 20 BEST SPORTS MOVIES</span>\n          </div>\n        </figure>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"sports\">\n        <h2>20 best<br>sports<br>movies</h2>\n        <div class=\"sub\">From Rocky to<br>Gregory’s Girl,<br>Senna to Zidane</div>\n        <div class=\"section-name\">In New Review</div>\n        <div class=\"sports-person placeholder\" aria-label=\"Woman footballer with ball\">\n          <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photo: woman footballer with ball]</span>\n          <div class=\"head\"></div>\n          <div class=\"body\"></div>\n          <div class=\"shorts\"></div>\n          <div class=\"leg one\"></div><div class=\"leg two\"></div>\n          <div class=\"sock one\"></div><div class=\"sock two\"></div>\n          <div class=\"ball\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"magazine\">\n        <figure class=\"mag-cover placeholder\" aria-label=\"The Observer Magazine cover featuring Daniel Mays\">\n          <div class=\"mag-name\">The Observer Magazine</div>\n          <div class=\"portrait\"></div>\n          <div class=\"cover-line\">At telly, [?] to step up</div>\n          <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photo: Daniel Mays]</span>\n        </figure>\n        <div class=\"promo-copy\">\n          <strong>Daniel Mays</strong>\n          On Mike Leigh,<br>\n          Michael Caine<br>\n          and Guys &amp; Dolls\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"section-name\">In the magazine</div>\n        <div class=\"barcode\" aria-label=\"Barcode 9 770029 771229\">\n          <span class=\"issue\">17</span>\n          <div class=\"bars\"></div>\n          <div class=\"number\">9 770029 771229</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"booze\">\n        <h2>Peak<br>booze</h2>\n        <div class=\"sub\">Why<br>Britain<br>has the<br>20-year<br>hangover<br>from hell</div>\n        <div class=\"section-name\">This section</div>\n        <div class=\"glass placeholder\" aria-label=\"Glass containing an alcoholic drink\">\n          <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photo: glass of alcohol]</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <div class=\"masthead\">\n      <div class=\"masthead-title\">The Observer</div>\n      <div class=\"publication\">\n        From £1.97 for<br>\n        subscribers<br>\n        <strong>www.observer.co.uk</strong><br>\n        Sunday 28 April 2024<br>\n        £4.00\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <h1 class=\"lead-headline\">Exclusive: top Tory MP defects<br>to Labour in fury at NHS crisis</h1>\n\n  <div class=\"news-grid\">\n    <article class=\"lead-area\">\n      <div class=\"lead-top\">\n        <aside class=\"summary\">\n          <ul>\n            <li>Ex-health minister slams ‘nationalist right’</li>\n            <li>‘Tories failing on improving care’</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"byline\">Toby Helm<em>Political Editor</em></div>\n          <div class=\"article-copy\">\n            <p>A Tory MP and former health minister has staged a dramatic defection to Labour, saying the Conservatives have become a “nationalist party of the right” that has abandoned compassion and no longer prioritises the NHS.</p>\n            <p>Dr Dan Poulter, the MP for Central Suffolk and North Ipswich, who works part-time as a mental health doctor in an NHS hospital, announced in an exclusive interview with the <em>Observer</em> that he was resigning as a Tory MP and would be taking the Labour whip until the next election.</p>\n            <p>He said he would not seek re-election to the House of Commons at the next general election. But, writing in today’s <em>Observer</em>, he says he envisages a role advising the Labour party on its policies on mental health while focusing more on his NHS work.</p>\n            <p>Poulter said his experiences on more than 20 night shifts over the last year in a severely overstretched accident and emergency department had been “truly life-changing” and persuaded him to defect to the only party he believed was now really committed to investing in improving the NHS.</p>\n          </div>\n        </aside>\n\n        <div class=\"lead-photo-block\">\n          <div class=\"photo-caption\">\n            <strong>Dan Poulter</strong>\n            filling out<br>\n            his party<br>\n            membership<br>\n            form with<br>\n            Labour MP<br>\n            Ellie Reeves.\n          </div>\n          <figure class=\"lead-photo placeholder\" aria-label=\"Dan Poulter and Ellie Reeves seated beneath a Labour sign\">\n            <div class=\"labour-sign\">Labour</div>\n            <div class=\"sofa\"></div>\n            <div class=\"person man\"></div>\n            <div class=\"person woman\"></div>\n            <div class=\"table\"></div>\n            <div class=\"mug one\">Lab</div>\n            <div class=\"mug two\">Lab</div>\n            <span class=\"placeholder-label\">[Photo: Dan Poulter filling out his party membership form with Labour MP Ellie Reeves]</span>\n          </figure>\n        </div>\n\n        <aside class=\"quote-box\">\n          <span class=\"quote-name\">Dan Poulter</span>\n          From the frontline I see the NHS desperately struggling. I’ve come to the conclusion the only cure is a Labour government\n          <span class=\"comment\">Comment, page 5</span>\n        </aside>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"lead-bottom\">\n        <div></div>\n        <div class=\"article-copy\">\n          <p>He said: “I could not go on as part of that. I have to be able to look my NHS colleagues in the eye, my patients in the eye and my constituents in the eye. And I know that the Conservative government has been failing on the thing I care about most, which is the NHS and its patients.”</p>\n          <p>The <em>Observer</em> understands that dis-</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"article-copy\">\n          <p>cussions between Poulter and senior Labour figures have been going on for many months at the highest levels about the timing and organisation of his likely defection, as well as advisory roles he could play in future in developing the party’s health policies, with the benefit of his firsthand inside knowledge.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"article-copy\">\n          <p>The defection has, however, been kept the tightest of secrets, with only half a dozen people in the party knowing it was coming before the <em>Observer</em> broke the news.</p>\n          <p>A one nation Tory on the left of the party, Poulter has regularly made his</p>\n          <div class=\"continued\">Continued on page 4 &nbsp;❯</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n\n    <article class=\"side-story\">\n      <h2>Government<br>was warned<br>about dirty<br>blood in 1970s</h2>\n      <div class=\"side-byline\">Jon Ungoed-Thomas<br>&amp; Robin McKie</div>\n      <div class=\"article-copy\">\n        <p>A commercial blood product at the centre of the biggest treatment scandal in the history of the NHS was approved for use after government officials were told convicts were among the paid donors and virus contamination “should be assumed”, corporate filings reveal.</p>\n        <p>The product, given to haemophiliacs in the 1970s and ’80s to enable their blood to clot, was injected into thousands of UK patients, including young children, who were then infected with HIV and hepatitis C.</p>\n        <p>A single batch could contain plasma from 20,000 donors harvested in US prisons and some of the poorest neighbourhoods of the US, where drug use and sexual infections were rife. One infected donation would contaminate the entire batch.</p>\n        <p>An inquiry led by Brian Langstaff will report next month on the scandal, which has killed about 3,000 people in the UK. He has already concluded “wrongs were done at individual, collective and systemic levels”.</p>\n        <p>The drug firm Bayer provided 7,000 documents to the inquiry, which reveals its subsidiary, Cutter Laboratories, warned in licensing application documents in the 1970s that its commercial blood product Koate, may contain viruses. It said: “Since the presence or absence of hepatitis virus in Koate</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"continued\">Continued on page 10 &nbsp;❯</div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>"
